{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were","id":1001141,"title":"Why weren't there Lunar Shards in the Jade Prison? What would change if there were?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-09T19:20:32-08:00","id":1001141,"title":"Why weren't there Lunar Shards in the Jade Prison? What would change if there were?","content":"Honestly, why weren't there both Lunar Exaltations and Solar Exaltations trapped in the Jade Prison? If they didn't trust the Lunar Exalted to help them in general, then wouldn't it be prudent to trap both sets of Exaltations at once? I don't by that it couldn't, if they made something capable of stopping the most powerful of Exaltations then certainly it could be made to trap both, even if it took a few more years to complete. At least a good number (30-100) of the Lunar Exalted would be attending the Solar Overlords during the Calibration.<br /> <br /> What difference would it make to Canon if there is say 100 lunar shards that were also trapped?<br /> <br /> Also I am a HUGE fan of the alternate origin of the Abyssal Shards as the Grave Goods created by the Jade Prison acting as tomb for the Solars and empowered by the vast wars and deaths creating them in a once in a Creation's event. In this version where there are also Lunar Shards in the Jade Prison as well... What do you do with them? What would a Death themed lunars be like? If the Abyssal Shards grabbed onto the Void as the Underworld Analog for the Unconquered Sun, what would the Underworld Analog for Luna be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:27:18-08:00","id":1001146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were#post1001141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, why weren't there both Lunar Exaltations and Solar Exaltations trapped in the Jade Prison? If they didn't trust the Lunar Exalted to help them in general, then wouldn't it be prudent to trap both sets of Exaltations at once? I don't by that it couldn't, if they made something capable of stopping the most powerful of Exaltations then certainly it could be made to trap both, even if it took a few more years to complete. At least a good number (30-100) of the Lunar Exalted would be attending the Solar Overlords during the Calibration.<br /> <br /> What difference would it make to Canon if there is say 100 lunar shards that were also trapped?<br /> <br /> Also I am a HUGE fan of the alternate origin of the Abyssal Shards as the Grave Goods created by the Jade Prison acting as tomb for the Solars and empowered by the vast wars and deaths creating them in a once in a Creation's event. In this version where there are also Lunar Shards in the Jade Prison as well... What do you do with them? What would a Death themed lunars be like? If the Abyssal Shards grabbed onto the Void as the Underworld Analog for the Unconquered Sun, what would the Underworld Analog for Luna be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Canonically, the Sidereals <u>tried</u> to capture the Lunar Exaltations in the Jade Prison, it just ..... well, didn't work. The Lunar Exaltations skipped right through the traps. Thematically appropriate for the Chosen of a God(ess) that emblemizes freedom and change.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:28:38-08:00","id":1001147,"title":"","content":"Underworld Luna? Maybe something with the rivers and oceanic bodies that now run through it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:34:55-08:00","id":1001148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001146#post1001146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canonically, the Sidereals <u>tried</u> to capture the Lunar Exaltations in the Jade Prison, it just ..... well, didn't work. The Lunar Exaltations skipped right through the traps. Thematically appropriate for the Chosen of a God(ess) that emblemizes freedom and change.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Canonically they raided Lytek's office/cabinet and placed them into the box. So the lunar shards slipped out after they tried to close the box? I don't remember that meantioned. Am I misremembering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:37:35-08:00","id":1001151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001148#post1001148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Canonically they raided Lytek's office/cabinet and placed them into the box. So the lunar shards slipped out after they tried to close the box? I don't remember that meantioned. Am I misremembering?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They did it to the <u>Solars</u>. As far as I remember, the Lunar Shards just NOPED right through, or reincarnated into new hosts immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:41:43-08:00","id":1001154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001148#post1001148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought Canonically they raided Lytek's office/cabinet and placed them into the box. So the lunar shards slipped out after they tried to close the box? I don't remember that meantioned. Am I misremembering?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e didn't explain it well, and it wasn't left particularly well-described in 1e. The Sidereals presumably had a hard enough time making a prison for 300 Solars that 400 Lunars was beyond their capability to produce given the constraints of time. They viewed Solars as tainted, and Lunars as just there. We might get a different reason when the Sidereals book comes out for 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:48:51-08:00","id":1001158,"title":"","content":"Lunars would probably be allowed to be important and do Big Things, had they been trapped, instead of being relegated to their second class citizen status due to needing a good setting for the return of Solars to matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:52:54-08:00","id":1001159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were#post1001141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't by that it couldn't, if they made something capable of stopping the most powerful of Exaltations then certainly it could be made to trap both, even if it took a few more years to complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why start off with a premise tailored to arguing with the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:52:56-08:00","id":1001160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001154#post1001154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We might get a different reason when the Sidereals book comes out for 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arg... when will that be? 2035?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:59:02-08:00","id":1001163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001159#post1001159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why start off with a premise tailored to arguing with the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is a &quot;What if&quot; question. And the because I was trying to minimize the &quot;because it did&quot; argument. Which has already come up twice now, so perhaps it was a miscalculation on my part to try to push it aside up front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T20:16:21-08:00","id":1001167,"title":"","content":"The real reason: because then Lunars would be truly pointless as setting elements.<br /> <br /> As it is, Lunars have only one actual purpose in the setting: to give the Wyld Hunt something to do between the Usurpation and the return of the Solars.<br /> <br /> Put them in the box and you might as well just delete them entirely.<br /> <br /> (TBH deleting the splat entirely is my preferred answer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T21:17:15-08:00","id":1001180,"title":"","content":"Trapping a small number of Lunar Exaltations might offer some interesting alternative story setups for Lunars, and particularly Lunar/Solar pairs, but it wouldn't really change the larger setting all that much. Trapping a large number would give them Realm a much freer hand in the world. Trap enough and we might see what sort of paradise the Dragon-Blooded could build if they didn't have to constantly deal with the threat of shape-shifting nihilistic terrorists who desire nothing less than the end of Civilization itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T22:37:45-08:00","id":1001204,"title":"","content":"Anyone have a good idea for an Underworld analog for Luna?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:13:53-08:00","id":1001233,"title":"","content":"If there's a volcano in your city, rumbling like it's about to reduce everything to ash, and gangs are fighting in the city streets, the volcano is probably considered the more urgent problem to deal with, even if the city officials <i>would</i> like it if they could just solve both problems.<br /> <br /> Also, the devs have weighed in on a very similar question previously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:24:11-08:00","id":1001235,"title":"","content":"Could be an interesting setting variant, since I don't think there's any real rationale why not other than &quot;They couldn't&quot; that's cast iron. I think all the implications of what the setting would be like are generally fairly obvious so I won't spell them out. <br /> <br /> One that isn't, totally, is you might see no Realm or an earlier collapse of the Realm as an institution as with no Lunars to oppose, the Wyld Hunt and Realm generally might lose Sidereal support and urgency. If Creation survived the alt-Great Contagion.<br /> <br /> Another, I think there'd generally be a good deal less functioning magic around in the world, even counting that you would lose out on destructive effects of Lunar warfare to the Realm. Though If the Lunars were imprisoned I don't think you'd see as big a difference with the canon world as between the Second Age and First Age again, because I would say the decline of the Second Age is a lot to do with the change in culture focus and &quot;fate&quot; (historical factors outside the control of people... even Sidereals) than which Exalted are around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:24:33-08:00","id":1001236,"title":"","content":"Why not make the infernals the corrupted Lunars? Deathlords promised a larger share of the exaltation than in normal canon, so they gave the 'weaker' lunar exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:47:44-08:00","id":1001240,"title":"","content":"The Nihilist Exalted are the broken, corrupted remnants of what were once Luna's Chosen. But gone are the days of their sacred hunts, of their grand rituals of spirit calling, of their culture, their poise, and their love. They have been twisted by their Neverborn masters, wretched remnants, mockeries of what once was. Where a Lunar would hunt a great beast for the thrill and joy of the act of hunting, the Nihilist kills the greats simply because it can. Where the Lunars entreated with gods as allies, the Nihilist perverts nature to call upon the dead. Where the Lunar once shapeshifted into the natural shapes of the world to gain their strengths, the Nihilist transforms into mockeries of the living, creatures no man should ever be forced to see. Where the Lunar once loved Creation, the Nihilist seeks to destroy it from within. Perhaps it is due to the madness the Lunars already hold in them, held over from Luna's madness - perhaps their exaltations were simply less resistant to the corruption. Regardless, these Exalted fully feel the madness of their masters.<br /> <br /> This Exalted type represents the insanity of the undying dead. Where the Abyssal Exalted represent the poise of the dead, their Nihilist siblings represent only the madness of death itself. This does not mean every one is a madman and unable to function - they simply hear the whispers of their masters in a way that would drive weaker men to the depths of madness. Where the Abyssal Exalted drag the dead back to life and turn the world into Shadowlands that mimic the Underworld, the Nihilist transforms themselves into monstrosities of the underworld that twist the mind of those who witness it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I dunno, came up with it in 5 minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:33:46-08:00","id":1001304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001163#post1001163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it is a &quot;What if&quot; question.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bVery well.<br /> <br /> \u200bGoing by what they're attributing to Lunars now, presumably you get a setting in which the strength of the Realm (possibly even the Shogunate, if a stronger version of it weathered the Contagion) is more widespread and the Dragon Blooded are more uncontested, on account of them still having a lot of their ancient stockpiles and arsenals, and not really having a major power to undermine them. Their scarcity issues are probably not as acute, so while their many territories might engage in war for a variety of reasons, it might be less often and less better.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe dynamic of the returned Exalted probably also differs, with perhaps a bit of emphasis on the idea of them being partners finding their way back to each other across the Ages and working together to renew the world, rather than the Solars returning to find that their old partners have undergone some drastic transformations in the interim.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't really see the Underworld as being particularly transformative to the Lunar concept, since I can't really see it as crossing over with it the way it can with the Solar culture hero, except for in superficial cosmetic ways.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough... while I think that the transformation into and association with animals is integral to Lunars, if I start with the stated mythology that part of that is Luna's tribute to Gaia, I suppose I could envision something in which the altered Lunar Exalted represent Luna's tribute to something from the Underworld. Hmmm...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T08:14:11-08:00","id":1001362,"title":"","content":"What about the Fair Folk? If the Lunars were gone for so long, wouldn't the raksha be much freer to invade Creation and cause trouble?<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe the stronger Realm could stand up to them just fine, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:28:01-08:00","id":1001379,"title":"","content":"It depends on whether you envision a setting in which the Lunars in particular have been a major force for keeping the Fair Folk out.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like the Shogunate material from First Edition, so I envision that period as having frequently come under attack by Wyld forces in the hundreds of thousands anyway. If I assume that's something the Lunars actually encouraged (at least indirectly, from frequently destroying First Age weapons), I could see the attacks as having been less frequent.<br /> <br /> \u200bDuring the time of the Realm, the Fair Folk numbers are crippled by what the Defence Grid did to them, so major attacks seem a lot less likely. Minor attacks are usually repelled by Realm legions (assuming they were cared about at all), and larger ones were also destroyed by the ancient weapons before they could get anywhere near a major target.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:47:03-08:00","id":1001434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were#post1001141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, why weren't there both Lunar Exaltations and Solar Exaltations trapped in the Jade Prison? If they didn't trust the Lunar Exalted to help them in general, then wouldn't it be prudent to trap both sets of Exaltations at once? I don't by that it couldn't, if they made something capable of stopping the most powerful of Exaltations then certainly it could be made to trap both, even if it took a few more years to complete. At least a good number (30-100) of the Lunar Exalted would be attending the Solar Overlords during the Calibration.<br /> <br /> What difference would it make to Canon if there is say 100 lunar shards that were also trapped?<br /> <br /> Also I am a HUGE fan of the alternate origin of the Abyssal Shards as the Grave Goods created by the Jade Prison acting as tomb for the Solars and empowered by the vast wars and deaths creating them in a once in a Creation's event. In this version where there are also Lunar Shards in the Jade Prison as well... What do you do with them? What would a Death themed lunars be like? If the Abyssal Shards grabbed onto the Void as the Underworld Analog for the Unconquered Sun, what would the Underworld Analog for Luna be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what do you know/remember about Prince Laashe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:39:53-08:00","id":1001500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001362#post1001362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Fair Folk? If the Lunars were gone for so long, wouldn't the raksha be much freer to invade Creation and cause trouble?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1001362#post1001362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, maybe the stronger Realm could stand up to them just fine, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>But\u2026?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:41:59-08:00","id":1002126,"title":"","content":"I like to think a lot of &quot;Why did the Sidereals do/not do X&quot; could be answered by &quot;because that is(n't) what the Vision of Bronze demanded.&quot;<br /> <br /> The guaranteed survival of Creation demanded, per Fate, the murder of all the Solar Exalted and the prevention of their reincarnation. It also <i>needed</i> the Dragon-Blooded to sit in charge afterward.<br /> <br /> If the Vision required the Lunars to be likewise locked away, the Sidereals likely would have found a way. As it stands, it didn't. This probably came as a relief to the Viziers; killing all the Solars was the hard part, sure, but needing to be thorough about both the Lawgivers and their God-Beast spouses would have been even more of a nightmare.<br /> <br /> But let's say Fate did demand the imprisoning of the Lunar Exalted. They are hunted and killed and largely gone from the setting in between point A (the Usurpation), and point B (the Present Day). This is honestly not terrible in and of itself since the majority of this history is &quot;Eh, things happen and go to shit, and the Empress rises to power in there somewhere.&quot; We'll also assume that something majorly setting-wrecking like &quot;the Fair Folk have nothing to hold them back and just curbstomp Creation&quot; happens, too. <br /> <br /> Where it starts to get tricky is they actually step on one of the Solar's narrative shtick now, that of the returning champion of antiquity. You could argue that Exigents are doing this now, but while the Exigence itself is a sort of old thing making its return, these new divine champions don't have the same sense of legacy. <br /> <br /> Without a mass exodus of the Lunar Exalted to the edge of the world, they don't have any elders anymore; the Sidereal Exalted become the only surviving host of Celestials with significant numbers who remember the First Age. Maybe--<i>maybe</i>--to highlight their ability to hide and blend in, they have one Elder somewhere, cagey and paranoid as hell, a skin-stealing horror no less messed up than Filial Wisdom, albeit better about hiding it. The Wyld Hunt is likely more aggressive, since they have a duty to hunt down the Lunars not just when they Exalt in their lands, or make themselves known. Driving them off is not an option.<br /> <br /> We probably drop Wyld Taint as a thing. I doubt many people miss it. The moonsilver tattoos are completely gone as a splat-wide thing, just because there's no reason for them to be everywhere if there was no lunar culture to create or maintain them. Lunars may also drop the Casteless/shifting Caste thing, since <br /> they no longer have the deep-rooted ties to the sorts of cultures where there's a sort of parallel between fixing of the caste and the rites of adulthood.<br /> <br /> In short, a lot of what does exist to separate the Solars from the Lunars and give the latter their narrative niche disappears. The Lunar Exalted maintain a little difference in flavor from their shapeshifting charms, and maybe Luna still tends to Exalt people from barbarian cultures, but the sense of real tradition is gone. Second Edition Lunars were occasionally accused of being Silver Solars; this just aggravates the problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T08:02:18-08:00","id":1002221,"title":"","content":"My preferred answer is that Luna keeps her Exaltations herself, since she appears to each Lunar, instead of letting Lytek handle them.<br /> <br /> And the Siddies weren't feeling froggy enough to go jumping on Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T08:48:10-08:00","id":1002235,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if it helps anyone but my Roaring20s setting has Lunars who appeared at the same time as the Solars during the First World War, a major part of what makes those two different is that the Solar Exalted tended to be the patriotic/idealist types who have been largely put to one side by the Dragon-Blooded establishment now that they've left a state of emergency. They're placed on a pedestal and expected not to disrupt the status quo. <br /> <br /> The Lunars are natural survivors with cannibalistic shapeshifting powers so they were never as beloved as the Solars, but in some ways that\u2019s helped them and allowed them to find niche roles (for example, several Lunars have flourished in the aviation industry) or mostly disappear off the Sidereal\u2019s radar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:45:56-08:00","id":1002287,"title":"","content":"I remember a fan project long ago that envisioned a few &quot;original recipe&quot; Lunar exaltations who had been inadvertently trapped in the Prison with the Solars. As such the never suffered exile to the Wyld or the breaking of the castes. In this particular case, the author chose to attribute things like the focus on totem and animal shapeshifting to the intervening years as well, and gave his version of &quot;original&quot; Lunars had more of a &quot;perfect self&quot; theme instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:28:46-08:00","id":1002423,"title":"","content":"This thread is giving me ideas of a new Shard where the Lunars also disappeared. It would mean that Creation would probably be smaller than it is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:04:36-08:00","id":1002442,"title":"","content":"I continue to dislike the idea that the big thing of the Lunars is fighting off the Fair Folk, for several reasons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T01:01:00-08:00","id":1002476,"title":"","content":"You and me both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T03:02:19-08:00","id":1002487,"title":"","content":"I've thought about the original question a bit more and here's what I came up with.<ul><li>The majority of the Wyld Hunt would be more focused on fighting Fae with only a small, elite group Anathema hunters. The return of the Solars and Lunars will therefore overwhelm the resources of the Wyld Hunt quite easily.</li> <li>Fae enclaves will definitely be larger and therefore a bigger threat to the returning Exalts.</li> <li>The Guild will be weaker since there would be less barbarian tribes to trade with for drugs and slaves.</li> <li>There would be no Second Age Silver Pact, so that means most if not all of the Lunars not caught would probably be Chimeras.</li> <li>Creation will probably stay roughly the same size considering the Jade monoliths would probably have taken less damage during the Shogunate.</li> <li>There would be a lot more Artifacts floating around.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T04:01:54-08:00","id":1002495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002487#post1002487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guild will be weaker since there would be less barbarian tribes to trade with for drugs and slaves\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Disputing this one. Welding tribes together and slamming them violently into the big empire's military hasn't exactly done much to improve the number of tribal peoples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-13-2016, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T05:05:43-08:00","id":1002503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002487#post1002487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The majority of the Wyld Hunt would be more focused on fighting Fae with only a small, elite group Anathema hunters. The return of the Solars and Lunars will therefore overwhelm the resources of the Wyld Hunt quite easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that does bring up a question; some Solars escaped the Jade Prison, so are any Lunars supposed to have done the same?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Fae enclaves will definitely be larger and therefore a bigger threat to the returning Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this so definite?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The Guild will be weaker since there would be less barbarian tribes to trade with for drugs and slaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one could easily argue that there would be <i>even more</i> &quot;barbarian&quot; people without Lunars to frequently be sending them off to die against the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]There would be no Second Age Silver Pact, so that means most if not all of the Lunars not caught would probably be Chimeras.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;not caught&quot; I take it you mean not imprisoned with the Solars?<br /> <br /> \u200bBut that still leaves the question of how their Castes change in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Creation will probably stay roughly the same size considering the Jade monoliths would probably have taken less damage during the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about when all of the people whose force of will and financial transactions died?<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, whether the preservation of the borders of the world has been attributed to patterned runes of human activity or jade monoliths, the majority of the damage is still attributed to the invasion of a billion Fair Folk.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T05:29:08-08:00","id":1002507,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF8C00\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002495#post1002495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disputing this one. Welding tribes together and slamming them violently into the big empire's military hasn't exactly done much to improve the number of tribal peoples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not talking about the Realm decimating the tribes, but rather the Fae.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002503#post1002503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, that does bring up a question; some Solars escaped the Jade Prison, so are any Lunars supposed to have done the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that some would (also, see below). Based on computations I and some forum members did back in 2e we estimated that about 10% of the Solars avoided getting imprisoned so why not the Lunars..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002503#post1002503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this so definite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the ranks of the Balorian Crusade would not have been decimated by encountering the Lunars on their way in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002503#post1002503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one could easily argue that there would be <i>even more</i> &quot;barbarian&quot; people without Lunars to frequently be sending them off to die against the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reasoning, much like what I answered to TheCountAlucard, is because of the Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002503#post1002503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By &quot;not caught&quot; I take it you mean not imprisoned with the Solars?<br /> <br /> \u200bBut that still leaves the question of how their Castes change in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, not imprisoned with the Solars.<br /> <br /> Ah! Here is where things enter house-rule areas. I am of the mind that Lunars never had a fixed Castes. They could change their Castes as befits their roles to be better able to support the Solars. Prolonged exposure to the Deep Wyld broke the Castes and later produced Chimeras. That means that the newly released Lunars would retain their old ability to choose Castes and hence no need for the tattoos.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002503#post1002503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about when all of the people whose force of will and financial transactions died?<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, whether the preservation of the borders of the world has been attributed to patterned runes of human activity or jade monoliths, the majority of the damage is still attributed to the invasion of a billion Fair Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically the original borders of creation was ringed by the monoliths and made stable. The Solars then expanded the boundaries of Creation beyond that ring. I posit that the Balorian Crusade caused the expanded boundaries to collapse, but since the ring of jade monoliths were not damaged during the Usurpation and Shogunate, Creation rebounded back to that border, albeit no longer stable.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":12288,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","user":"Mal'akh","date":". 11-13-2016, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T06:06:38-08:00","id":1002511,"title":"","content":"Why would the fae do more harm to barbarians in your scenario?<br /> <br /> The Lunars had no more meaningful an impact on the Balorian Crusade than a sheet of paper does on a hurricane.<br /> <br /> Also, the Balorian Crusade was one event, one that actually predates the Guild by quite a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-13-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T06:27:14-08:00","id":1002515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002442#post1002442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I continue to dislike the idea that the big thing of the Lunars is fighting off the Fair Folk, for several reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div> I certainly think we should revisit this when the Lunars book comes out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T08:53:50-08:00","id":1002540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002507#post1002507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Because the ranks of the Balorian Crusade would not have been decimated by encountering the Lunars on their way in.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think the results of such would be insignificant compared to what the Realm Defence Grid did to them.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough we're back into the question of why Lunars, specifically, are supposed to be any more significant as a force fighting off the Fair Folk during the Contagion or that threaten outlying tribes compared to anything else in Creation.<br /> <br /> \u200bEspecially since the new Edition is likely to portray the Lunars during both stages as a lot more focused on the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn that note, I posit that if there are fewer Lunars during the Shogunate, then there are a lot more Dragon Blooded with ancient mystical weapons in the vanguard against the invaders, so it largely evens out.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, I suppose that my suggestion of the Dragon Blooded controlling more of the world also has the consequence of fewer outlying tribes, just for different reasons and with different implications.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically the original borders of creation was ringed by the monoliths and made stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, I'm not sure about canon, but either way I read your comment as being about Creation being the size it was during the Shogunate, and that appears to have been mistaken on my part.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T02:32:39-08:00","id":1002804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002511#post1002511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the fae do more harm to barbarians in your scenario?<br /> <br /> The Lunars had no more meaningful an impact on the Balorian Crusade than a sheet of paper does on a hurricane.<br /> <br /> Also, the Balorian Crusade was one event, one that actually predates the Guild by quite a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous canon the Lunars cultivated the barbarians, without the Lunars the barbarians are more vulnerable to the depradations of the Fae.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002540#post1002540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOn that note, I posit that if there are fewer Lunars during the Shogunate, then there are a lot more Dragon Blooded with ancient mystical weapons in the vanguard against the invaders, so it largely evens out.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, I suppose that my suggestion of the Dragon Blooded controlling more of the world also has the consequence of fewer outlying tribes, just for different reasons and with different implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that line of reasoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1002540#post1002540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell, I'm not sure about canon, but either way I read your comment as being about Creation being the size it was during the Shogunate, and that appears to have been mistaken on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! You thought I meant a DotFA kind of Creation. No, I was thinking of Creation as presented now. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T03:45:28-08:00","id":1002818,"title":"","content":"By &quot;previous canon,&quot; do you mean &quot;2e and only 2e?&quot; Because prior to that (i.e., 1e), they shaped them <i>to fight the Realm</i>, and after that (i.e., Ex3), they shaped them <i>to fight the Realm</i>. It's not a healthy relationship; the Lunars prop themselves up as gods of these fringe cultures in the hopes that <i>this</i> wave of human meat is the one that finally jams and breaks the Realm's military grinder. Sure, this occasionally entails the Lunar protecting them from Fair Folk, but only so the Lunar can then send an entire generation off to be killed.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to point out that there were still hundreds of millions of Fair Folk and only ~300-400 Lunars. Much like in the &quot;How do mortals survive&quot; thread, mortal communities by and large get by not by having a supernatural protector stand between them and the horrors, but by not bedding down right next to the horrors in the first place (and also the horrors not being mindless, faceless hordes who just want to see absolutely everything burned to the ground and salted).<br /> <br /> Also, why Fair Folk in particular? What's so special about them as antagonists that the Lunars supposedly throw themselves at them to save these mortal communities, and not gods, elementals, the dead, and even other mortals?<br /> <br /> (As a last aside, most of the definitions of &quot;cultivate&quot; indicate that you're caring for something <i>so you can use it for something</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-14-2016, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T05:56:26-08:00","id":1002850,"title":"","content":"Wait... weren't we discussing what would happen if the Lunars got imprisoned in the Jade Prison? That's the reason why I posted what I have been posting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T07:44:53-08:00","id":1002879,"title":"","content":"Yes, but you posited that there would be <i>less</i> barbarians by dint of Lunars not being there to protect them from the Fair Folk, but <i>as a splat</i>, &quot;protecting barbarians from the Fair Folk&quot; is not a Lunar <i>thing</i>, and &quot;sending barbarians off in suicidal attacks against the Realm&quot; <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that absent the Lunars, things would be hunky-dory between barbarians and the Realm and the Fair Folk, but the two former groups would doubtless be better off by dint of being in less and less bloody conflicts with each other, and the last would be in pretty much the exact same boat it's already in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-14-2016, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:05:04-08:00","id":1003586,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the realm still be in bloody conflict with barbarians, just more successfully? I mean their whole schtick is that everyone should do as they say without questioning it. That does not lend itself to positive foreign relations.<br /> <br /> If anything with out the lunars I imagine the realm and the shogunate before them would be much weaker and more prone to open schism and divide since there'd be less external pressure.<br /> <br /> In fact without the lunars to provide that constant unifying threat to DB-ruled civilizations I'd imagine that at some point they'd have split into multiple empires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:08:11-08:00","id":1008046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1003586#post1003586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the realm still be in bloody conflict with barbarians, just more successfully?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you play basketball against someone and they annihilate you 254-0, how do you feel about immediately challenging them again? Now, what if they only won by two points instead?<br /> <br /> A more victorious Realm is less likely to be challenged again in short order than a Realm that is perceived as having just squeaked by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1003586#post1003586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean their whole schtick is that everyone should do as they say without questioning it. That does not lend itself to positive foreign relations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only the president-elect would internalize this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1003586#post1003586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything with out the lunars I imagine the realm and the shogunate before them would be much weaker and more prone to open schism and divide since there'd be less external pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but I doubt it. For one thing, the Shogunate was <i>already</i> a period of schism and divide. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1001141-why-weren-t-there-lunar-shards-in-the-jade-prison-what-would-change-if-there-were?p=1003586#post1003586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact without the lunars to provide that constant unifying threat to DB-ruled civilizations I'd imagine that at some point they'd have split into multiple empires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the nature of the Empress, I'm not buying this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:18:30-08:00","id":1009000,"title":"","content":"The main argument against it is that it would make Lunars more similar to Solars, narratively, which they don't need - right now, the fact that Lunars have been around for 1500 years is the main thing that gives them a unique place in the setting. Without that they'd just be a slightly different color of Anathema with somewhat different abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}